      trivia: "In 1920 it is credited with introducing the industry's first three-stick foil pouch, the beginning of the cigar's change from an article of the wooden box to one 'carried about and bought on the spot'. In the 1930s it became America's largest five-cent cigar, selling 520 million sticks a year, and in the radio broadcasts of the New York Yankees a home run was called a 'White Owl Wallop'. An advertisement featuring Babe Ruth and his wife together also appeared in 1938."
